# AI Repo Judge configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in this folder:  cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in only what you need. Everything is optional: with no keys the judge
#    still runs its static analysis (LLM-scored parts are then left out).
# 3. NEVER commit your real '.env'.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- LLM review (free tiers work) ---
# Primary provider and fallbacks, tried in order: groq | gemini | openrouter | ollama | custom
LLM_PROVIDER=groq
LLM_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS=gemini

# Groq: free key at https://console.groq.com (8K tokens/min, 200K tokens/day on the free plan)
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Google AI Studio: free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (GOOGLE_API_KEY is also accepted)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest

# OpenRouter (free models end in :free)
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b:free

# Local models via Ollama (no key; run `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b` first)
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://example.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
# LLM_MODEL=model-name

# Per-provider limits used by the client-side rate limiter (defaults match free tiers)
# GROQ_TPM=8000
# GROQ_RPM=30

# --- GitHub ---
# Optional. Raises the API limit for PR metadata from 60 to 5,000 requests/hour.
# A fine-grained token with no extra permissions (public read-only) is enough.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here
# JUDGE_REPO=gdgcblr/open-source-agents

# --- Run defaults (all optional) ---
# JUDGE_LLM=auto            # auto | on | off | mock
# JUDGE_OUT=./data          # where dashboard data is written
# JUDGE_CACHE=./.cache      # git mirror, PR workspaces and stored evaluations

# --- Storage ---
# local (JSON files in ./data) or firestore (pip install -e ".[firebase]")
JUDGE_STORE=local
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json
